# LoT Broker Configuration
# =============================================================================
# This file configures the MQTT broker connection for LoT notebooks.
# Copy this file to .broker (without .example) and modify as needed.
#
# Format: mqtt://[username:password@]host:port
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 1: Local Development (default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connect to local Coreflux broker running in Docker
mqtt://localhost:1883

# With authentication (recommended for production):
# mqtt://admin:coreflux@localhost:1883

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 2: Public Cloud Broker
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connect to Coreflux public broker for cloud demos
# WARNING: All messages are visible to everyone on this broker!
# mqtt://iot.coreflux.cloud:1883

# With TLS encryption (recommended):
# mqtts://iot.coreflux.cloud:8883

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option 3: Secondary Broker (for bridge testing)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connect to local Mosquitto broker
# mqtt://localhost:1884
